Panama Foundation Establishment (Fixed in USD)

We will establish a Panama Private Interest Foundation to hold and manage assets on behalf of the nominated beneficiaries.

This includes:

(a) Preparation and filing of the Foundation Charter with the Public Registry of Panama, including the name, purpose, initial assets, and governing provisions;

(b) Preparation of the Foundation Regulations, setting out the rules governing the management of the foundation, the rights of the beneficiaries, and the powers of the Foundation Council;

(c) Appointment of the Nominee Foundation Council members and the resident agent in Panama;

(d) Nomination of the beneficiaries and any protector, including the terms on which distributions may be made;

(e) Ensuring the foundation is compliant with Panamanian regulatory requirements; and

(f) Providing all formation documents, certificates, and records for your files.

Fee is inclusive of first year compliance and registered agent fees, as follows:

- Cadena International fee: $5,000
- Panama registry and local agent fee: $1,700
- Nominee council fee: $1.500

Share Sale Agreement (Fixed)

We will prepare a Share Sale Agreement to facilitate the sale and transfer of shares in XXX from the seller to the buyer.
The agreement will cover the following key matters:

(a) The sale and purchase of the shares, including the number of shares, the purchase price, and the payment terms;

(b) Representations and warranties given by the seller in relation to the shares and the company, including as to ownership, financial position, and the absence of undisclosed liabilities;

(c) Conditions precedent to completion, if applicable, including any regulatory approvals or third-party consents required;

(d) Completion mechanics, including the delivery of share transfers, updated registers, and director resignation or appointment (if relevant);

(e) Post-completion obligations, including any restraint of trade, non-compete, or transitional arrangements; and

(f) Indemnities and limitations on liability.

This fee includes one round of amendments, further amendments will be considered out of scope.

Contractor Agreement (Estimated)

We will prepare a Contractor Agreement tailored to your requirements for the engagement of a contractor by XXX Pty Ltd. The agreement will include robust confidentiality provisions to protect the company's sensitive information.

The agreement will cover:

(a) The scope of the services to be provided, including the specific deliverables, timeframes, and any reporting obligations;

(b) The fees payable to the contractor, including the rate, payment schedule, and any reimbursable expenses;

(c) The term of the engagement, including the start date, duration, and the circumstances in which either party may terminate the agreement;

(d) Confidentiality obligations requiring the contractor to protect the company's confidential information and trade secrets, including restrictions on the use, disclosure, and reproduction of confidential material both during and after the engagement;

(e) Intellectual property provisions to ensure any work product, inventions, or materials created during the engagement are owned by the company;

(f) The relationship between the parties, including confirmation that the contractor is an independent contractor and not an employee; and

(g) Liability and indemnity provisions, including the contractor's obligation to indemnify the company for any loss arising from a breach of the agreement, including a breach of the confidentiality obligations.

This fee includes one round of amendments.

Master Service Agreement (Fixed)

We will prepare a Master Service Agreement for COMPANY Pty Ltd tailored to the provision of digital asset brokerage services in Australia.

The agreement will cover:

(a) The scope of the brokerage services to be provided, including the types of digital assets covered, execution terms, and any limitations on the services;

(b) Client onboarding requirements, including identity verification and AML/CTF obligations;

(c) Fees, commissions, and payment terms, including how transaction fees are calculated and when they are payable;

(d) Custody and settlement arrangements, including how client digital assets are held, transferred, and settled;

(e) Risk disclosures and client acknowledgements, including the volatility and nature of digital assets;

(f) Liability and indemnity provisions, including limitations on the company's liability for market losses, system outages, or third-party failures;

(g) Confidentiality and data protection obligations; and

(h) Termination provisions, including the process for closing client accounts and returning any digital assets or funds held.

This fee includes two rounds of amendments.

Small Business CGT Concessions Advice (Estimated)

We will prepare tax advice on satisfying the requirements to access the small business CGT concessions under Division 152 in connection with the sale of the Intellectual Property (IP) rights.

We will advise on:

(a) whether the basic conditions for relief are met, including the maximum net asset value test and the active asset test;

(b) which of the four small business CGT concessions are available to you (15-year exemption, 50% active asset reduction, retirement exemption, and/or small business rollover);

(c) how the concessions interact and can be applied to minimise the capital gain;

(d) opportunities to contribute amounts to superannuation in connection with the retirement exemption or 15-year exemption; and

(e) a step plan setting out the actions required to execute, including any pre-sale restructuring.

The deliverable is a detailed letter of advice.

Division 7A Review & Strategies (estimated)

We will review COMPANY structure to identify the sources of  Division 7A issues, and provide high-level strategies to improve the tax efficiency of how funds move between entities in the group.

We will advise on:

(a) Opportunities to restructure existing arrangements to reduce or remove any Division 7A exposure;

(b) Strategies to improve how profits, distributions, and capital flow between the entities in the group in a tax-effective way; 

We will outline our findings in a high-level summary.
